== Prominent National Parks and Biosphere Reserves
- *Jim Corbett National Park (Uttarakhand):* India's oldest national park (established in 1936 as Hailey National Park); launch site of Project Tiger (1973).
- *Kaziranga National Park (Assam):* UNESCO World Heritage Site hosting two-thirds of the world's Great One-Horned Rhinoceroses.
- *Sundarbans National Park (West Bengal):* World's largest mangrove forest delta; home of the Royal Bengal Tiger.
- *Gir National Park (Gujarat):* The sole surviving wild sanctuary for the Asiatic Lion (*Panthera leo persica*).
- *Keibul Lamjao National Park (Manipur):* The world's only *floating national park*, situated upon Loktak Lake, preserving the endangered Sangai brow-antlered deer on floating vegetation masses (*phumdis*).

= Science, Defense, and Modern Milestones

== The Indian Space Exploration Architecture (ISRO)
Headquartered in Bengaluru (established on *15 August 1969* under Dr. Vikram Sarabhai):
- *Chandrayaan-3 (2023):* Historic lunar mission comprising the *Vikram lander* and *Pragyan rover*. On *23 August 2023*, India became the first nation to achieve a successful soft-landing near the lunar south pole. The landing site was officially named *"Shiv Shakti Point"*, and 23 August was declared *National Space Day*.
- *Aditya-L1 (2023):* India's first dedicated space-based observatory placed into a halo orbit around the Sun-Earth *Lagrangian Point 1 (L1)* to study solar flares, coronal mass ejections, and the solar corona.
- *Gaganyaan Program:* India's flagship human spaceflight mission aiming to demonstrate indigenous crewed orbital capability in low Earth orbit.

== Strategic Defense & Indigenous Missiles (DRDO)
Developed largely under the Integrated Guided Missile Development Programme (IGMDP) spearheaded by Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam:
- *PRITHVI:* Surface-to-surface short-range ballistic missile.
- *AGNI:* Surface-to-surface medium to intercontinental ballistic missile series (Agni-V with range $> 5,000 text(" km")$).
- *TRISHUL / AKASH:* Surface-to-air defense missile systems.
- *NAG:* Third-generation "fire-and-forget" anti-tank guided missile.
- *BRAHMOS:* Supersonic cruise missile jointly developed by India (DRDO) and Russia (NPO Mashinostroyeniya), capable of land, sea, sub-sea, and air launches.

== The Award Pyramid of the Republic of India
- *Civilian Honours:* Instituted in 1954:
  1. *Bharat Ratna:* Highest civilian honour (first recipients in 1954: C. Rajagopalachari, Dr. S. Radhakrishnan, Dr. C.V. Raman).
  2. *Padma Vibhushan:* For exceptional and distinguished service.
  3. *Padma Bhushan:* For distinguished service of a high order.
  4. *Padma Shri:* For distinguished service in any field.
- *Military Gallantry Honours (Wartime vs Peacetime):*
  - *Wartime Gallantry:* *Param Vir Chakra (PVC)* (Highest military decoration; first recipient Major Somnath Sharma) $arrow$ Maha Vir Chakra $arrow$ Vir Chakra.
  - *Peacetime Gallantry:* *Ashok Chakra* (Highest peacetime bravery award) $arrow$ Kirti Chakra $arrow$ Shaurya Chakra.

