#cheatsheet-box(title: "Master Strategy Cheatsheet — General Knowledge & Current Affairs")[
  *1. Constitutional Quick Index:*
  - *Part III (Fundamental Rights):* Articles 14–32 (Enforceable/Justiciable).
  - *Part IV (DPSP):* Articles 36–51 (Non-justiciable; Art 44 = Uniform Civil Code).
  - *Part IVA (Fundamental Duties):* Article 51A (11 duties; 42nd & 86th Amendments).
  - *Part XVIII (Emergencies):* Art 352 (National), Art 356 (President's Rule), Art 360 (Financial — never used).

  *2. UN & Global Agency Locations:*
  - *New York:* UN Headquarters, UNICEF.
  - *Geneva:* WHO, WTO, ILO, UNHCR, WIPO.
  - *Paris:* UNESCO, OECD.
  - *Washington, D.C.:* World Bank, IMF.
  - *The Hague:* International Court of Justice (ICJ).
  - *Rome:* Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), World Food Programme (WFP).

  *3. The 5-Field Daily Event Deconstruction Grid:*
  $ "Event" arrow "WHAT (Core)" + "WHEN (Date)" + "WHERE / WHO (Agency)" + "WHY (Significance)" + "STATIC LINK" $
]

#exception-box(title: "The Seven Fatal CUET Traps in General Knowledge")[
  1. *The Head of State vs Head of Government Confusion:* Mistaking the President (Head of the State / Constitutional Head) for the Prime Minister (Head of the Government / Executive Head).
  2. *The Article 32 vs Article 226 Jurisdiction Slip:* Forgetting that Supreme Court writ jurisdiction is under Article 32 (only for Fundamental Rights), while High Courts issue writs under Article 226 (for Fundamental Rights and other legal rights).
  3. *The Geographical Superlative Misplacement:* Confusing K2 (in PoK/Karakoram) with Kanchenjunga (the highest mountain peak in undisputed Indian territory).
  4. *The Award Pyramid Category Swap:* Choosing Bharat Ratna as a sports or military award. Bharat Ratna is India's highest civilian honour; Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna is highest for sports; Param Vir Chakra is highest for military gallantry.
  5. *The Classical Dance Origin Scramble:* Confusing Kathakali (Kerala dance-drama) with Kathak (North Indian classical dance), or Mohiniyattam (Kerala) with Kuchipudi (Andhra Pradesh).
  6. *The Bretton Woods vs UN Headquarters Swap:* Stating Geneva or New York as headquarters of the IMF/World Bank instead of Washington, D.C.
  7. *The Blind Guessing Negative Penalty:* Wildly guessing on obscure factual questions. If you cannot eliminate at least two options, leave the question unattempted to shield your score against the $-1$ deduction.
]

