= Practice Questions — Part 1: Polity & Constitution (Q1 to Q5)

#mcq(1, [Which Constitutional Amendment Act added the terms "Socialist", "Secular", and "Integrity" to the Preamble of the Constitution of India?], (
  [44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978],
  [42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976],
  [86th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2002],
  [73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992],
))
#solution(1, [The 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act of 1976 (frequently termed the "Mini-Constitution") inserted the words *Socialist, Secular,* and *Integrity* into the Preamble. The 44th Amendment restored civil liberties post-emergency; the 86th added Article 21A (Education); the 73rd constitutionalized Panchayati Raj.], answer: [B])

#mcq(2, [Which article of the Indian Constitution was characterized by Dr. B.R. Ambedkar as the "very soul of the Constitution and the very heart of it"?], (
  [Article 14 (Equality before Law)],
  [Article 19 (Right to Freedom)],
  [Article 21 (Protection of Life and Personal Liberty)],
  [Article 32 (Right to Constitutional Remedies)],
))
#solution(2, [Dr. B.R. Ambedkar designated Article 32 (Right to Constitutional Remedies) as the "Heart and Soul" of the Constitution because without legal remedies to enforce Fundamental Rights via judicial writs, fundamental guarantees would be rendered meaningless.], answer: [D])

#mcq(3, [Which of the following bodies in India is an EXECUTIVE body created via Cabinet Resolution, and NOT a constitutional or statutory authority?], (
  [Election Commission of India],
  [NITI Aayog],
  [Comptroller and Auditor General of India],
  [Union Public Service Commission],
))
#solution(3, [NITI Aayog (National Institution for Transforming India) was constituted on 1 January 2015 via an executive resolution of the Union Cabinet, replacing the Planning Commission. The Election Commission (Art 324), CAG (Art 148), and UPSC (Art 315) are established directly by the Constitution.], answer: [B])

#mcq(4, [Under the Indian Constitution, which Fundamental Rights CANNOT be suspended even during the proclamation of a National Emergency under Article 352?], (
  [Article 20 and Article 21],
  [Article 19 and Article 20],
  [Article 14 and Article 19],
  [Article 21 and Article 22],
))
#solution(4, [By virtue of the 44th Constitutional Amendment Act (1978), the right to protection in respect of conviction for offences (*Article 20*) and the right to life and personal liberty (*Article 21*) cannot be suspended under any circumstances, including a National Emergency under Article 352 (Option A).], answer: [A])

#mcq(5, [The Fundamental Duties of Indian citizens were incorporated into Part IVA of the Constitution based on the recommendations of which committee?], (
  [Sarkaria Commission],
  [Verma Committee],
  [Swaran Singh Committee],
  [Kothari Commission],
))
#solution(5, [The Swaran Singh Committee was appointed by the Union Government in 1976 to assess constitutional amendments, and its recommendations directly resulted in the insertion of Fundamental Duties (Article 51A) via the 42nd Amendment Act. Sarkaria examined Center-State relations; Kothari addressed education reform.], answer: [C])

