#mcq(8, [Which of the following mountain peaks represents the highest mountain summit located within undisputed Indian territory?], (
  [Mount Everest],
  [K2 (Godwin-Austen)],
  [Nanda Devi],
  [Kanchenjunga],
))
#solution(8, [Kanchenjunga (8,586 m), situated along the Sikkim-Nepal border, is the highest peak located within undisputed Indian borders. Mount Everest (8,848 m) lies in Nepal; K2 (8,611 m) lies in the Karakoram range in Pakistan-occupied Kashmir (PoK); Nanda Devi (7,816 m) is entirely within India but lower.], answer: [D])

#mcq(9, [The world's only floating national park, Keibul Lamjao National Park, famous for preserving the endangered brow-antlered deer (Sangai), is situated in which Indian state?], (
  [Assam],
  [Manipur],
  [Meghalaya],
  [Mizoram],
))
#solution(9, [Keibul Lamjao National Park is situated on Loktak Lake in the Bishnupur district of Manipur. It is characterized by floating decomposing plant biomass termed *phumdis*, providing the exclusive wild habitat for the endangered Eld's deer subspecies (*Sangai*).], answer: [B])

#mcq(10, [Which peninsular Indian river is famously designated as "Dakshin Ganga" due to its extensive basin, spiritual reverence, and length?], (
  [Krishna],
  [Cauvery],
  [Godavari],
  [Mahanadi],
))
#solution(10, [The Godavari River (1,465 km) is the longest river in Peninsular India and second longest in India after the Ganga; because of its vast size, age, and spiritual sanctity, it is termed *Dakshin Ganga* (Ganges of the South). Cauvery is sometimes referred to as the Ganga of the South due to ritual holiness, but Godavari is the official geographical Dakshin Ganga.], answer: [C])

