= Practice Questions — Part 3: Culture, Science & Awards (Q11 to Q15)

#mcq(11, [Sattriya, one of the eight classical dance forms of India recognized by the Sangeet Natak Akademi, originated in which state as an integral part of the Bhakti movement?], (
  [Odisha],
  [Manipur],
  [Assam],
  [Tripura],
))
#solution(11, [Sattriya originated in the 15th century in Assam, propagated by the revered Vaishnavite scholar, poet, and saint-reformer *Srimanta Sankardev* inside Vaishnava monasteries known as *Sattras*. It was officially designated a classical dance by the Sangeet Natak Akademi in 2000.], answer: [C])

#mcq(12, [On which date is National Space Day celebrated annually in India to commemorate the historic soft-landing of the Chandrayaan-3 lander on the Moon?], (
  [14 July],
  [23 August],
  [2 September],
  [22 October],
))
#solution(12, [The Government of India declared *23 August* as *National Space Day* to commemorate the triumphant soft-landing of Chandrayaan-3's Vikram lander near the lunar south pole on 23 August 2023, making India the fourth nation to land on the Moon and first in the polar region.], answer: [B])

#mcq(13, [Who among the following was NOT among the first three recipients of India's highest civilian honour, the Bharat Ratna, when it was instituted in 1954?], (
  [C. Rajagopalachari],
  [Dr. S. Radhakrishnan],
  [Dr. C.V. Raman],
  [Jawaharlal Nehru],
))
#solution(13, [In 1954, the inaugural Bharat Ratna was conferred upon three eminent citizens: C. Rajagopalachari (last Governor-General of India), Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan (first Vice President), and Dr. C.V. Raman (Nobel laureate physicist). Jawaharlal Nehru was awarded the Bharat Ratna later in 1955.], answer: [D])

#mcq(14, [Aditya-L1, India's premier dedicated scientific space observatory, was launched by ISRO to study solar dynamics from a halo orbit around which point?], (
  [Sun-Earth Lagrangian Point 1 (L1)],
  [Earth-Moon Lagrangian Point 1 (L1)],
  [Sun-Earth Lagrangian Point 2 (L2)],
  [Geostationary Transfer Orbit],
))
#solution(14, [Aditya-L1 was positioned in a halo orbit around the Sun-Earth *Lagrangian Point 1 (L1)*, situated roughly 1.5 million kilometers from Earth. This location affords an uninterrupted, continuous view of the Sun without occultation or eclipses.], answer: [A])

#mcq(15, [The premier literary award in India, the Jnanpith Award, instituted in 1961, was first conferred in 1965 upon which renowned writer?], (
  [Rabindranath Tagore],
  [G. Sankara Kurup],
  [Munshi Premchand],
  [K.V. Puttappa (Kuvempu)],
))
#solution(15, [The inaugural Jnanpith Award was conferred in 1965 upon celebrated Malayalam poet *G. Sankara Kurup* for his poetry anthology *Odakkuzhal* (The Bamboo Flute). Tagore won the Nobel in 1913; Premchand passed away in 1936 before Jnanpith was founded.], answer: [B])
